OBSOLETE -- disabled 2026-08-06, kept for provenance.

This removed the "${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/../cmake" include from
clang's CMakeLists.txt, which was needed when buildroot built clang from the
standalone clang-<version>.src.tar.xz: that tarball has no sibling cmake/
directory, so the include failed.

Buildroot now builds from the llvm-project MONOREPO
(package/llvm-project/clang, CLANG_SUBDIR = clang).  Patches apply at the monorepo
root, so "a/CMakeLists.txt" no longer resolves -- the file is at
a/clang/CMakeLists.txt -- which is the visible failure:

  Applying 001-fix-cmake.patch using patch:
  can't find file to patch at input line 5

Retargeting it would be wrong, not just unnecessary.  The monorepo DOES ship
cmake/ beside clang/, so "../cmake" now resolves; and LLVM_COMMON_CMAKE_UTILS,
which this patch deletes, is still used further down the same file (for
LLVMVersion.cmake and the module search path).  Removing it would break the
build rather than fix it.

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt.new
index 5f2b7f064d..f74296be34 100644
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt.new
@@ -1,11 +1,5 @@
 cmake_minimum_required(VERSION 3.20.0)
 
-if(NOT DEFINED LLVM_COMMON_CMAKE_UTILS)
-  set(LLVM_COMMON_CMAKE_UTILS ${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/../cmake)
-endif()
-include(${LLVM_COMMON_CMAKE_UTILS}/Modules/CMakePolicy.cmake
-  NO_POLICY_SCOPE)
-
 # If we are not building as a part of LLVM, build Clang as an
 # standalone project, using LLVM as an external library:
 if(CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR STREQUAL CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR)
@@ -107,10 +107,6 @@ if(CLANG_BUILT_STANDALONE)
       endif()
     endif()
 
-    if (NOT TARGET llvm_gtest)
-        message(FATAL_ERROR "llvm-gtest not found. Please install llvm-gtest or disable tests with -DLLVM_INCLUDE_TESTS=OFF")
-    endif()
-
     if(LLVM_LIT)
       # Define the default arguments to use with 'lit', and an option for the user
       # to override.
